# Development — Epics & Stories

This phase decomposes the approved design into units of work small enough to
implement test-first. Epics group stories; each story becomes one or more
tasks.md entries with the boundary, requirement IDs, and RED→GREEN sub-tasks
csdd validates.

## Goal

Produce `specs/<feature>/epics.md` (the human-readable breakdown) and a filled,
validated, approved csdd `tasks.md` whose annotations let `tdd-cycle` pick up any
single task with full context.

## Default Operation Mode

Plan-first. You present the epic/story breakdown for confirmation before
generating tasks. The deliverable is a validated `tasks.md`, not code.

## Collect Inputs First

- Is the design phase approved? `csdd spec status <feature>` — if not, run
  `dev-architecture` first.
- What are the Boundary Map component names from `design.md`? (tasks reference
  them verbatim as `_Boundary:_`.)
- What is the natural slicing — by user journey, by capability, by risk-first?

## Execution Workflow

### 1) Define epics
Group the design's capabilities into epics (each a shippable slice of value).
Fill `assets/epics-template.md`. Order epics so the riskiest/foundational work
comes first.

### 2) Write stories
For each epic, write stories using `assets/story-template.md`: as-a/I-want/so-that,
acceptance criteria (mapped to requirement IDs), and the boundary it touches.
Each story must be implementable in a focused sitting.

### 3) Fold into csdd tasks.md
- `csdd spec generate <feature> --artifact tasks`.
- Translate stories into tasks following `.claude/rules/tasks-generation.md`:
  - Every parent task carries `_Boundary: <Component>_` (matching `design.md`).
  - Each behavior is a **RED** sub-task immediately followed by a **GREEN** one.
  - Every leaf has `_Requirements: <IDs>_`; cross-boundary order uses `_Depends:_`.
  - Mark parallel-safe tasks `(P)`; no two `(P)` tasks may share a boundary.

### 4) Gate it
- `csdd spec validate <feature>` (checks every leaf has `_Requirements:_`, every
  `(P)` has a `_Boundary:_`, `_Depends:_` IDs exist, no two `(P)` share a
  boundary). Fix every issue.
- `csdd spec approve <feature> --phase tasks`.

## Gotchas

- A story you cannot write acceptance criteria for is not ready — it is a
  research task. Split it.
- `_Boundary:_` values must match `design.md` component names exactly, or
  validation fails. Do not invent new names here.
- Keep sub-tasks to 1–3 hours. "Implement the feature" is not a task.
- Stories trace to requirement IDs; a story with no requirement is scope creep —
  route it back to discovery.

## Verification Before Reporting

- Run: `csdd spec validate <feature>`.
- Check: it exits 0; every story maps to ≥1 task; every behavior has a RED+GREEN
  pair; tasks phase is approved.
- If blocked: if a requirement has no implementable story, the design is
  incomplete — return to `dev-architecture`.

## Completion Criteria
- [ ] `specs/<feature>/epics.md` lists epics and implementation-ready stories.
- [ ] `tasks.md` is filled with correct `_Boundary:_`, `_Requirements:_`,
      `_Depends:_`, `(P)`, and RED→GREEN sub-tasks.
- [ ] `csdd spec validate <feature>` exits 0 and the tasks phase is approved.
- [ ] Every story traces to a requirement; every requirement is covered by tasks.

## References

- Use `assets/epics-template.md` for the epic breakdown.
- Use `assets/story-template.md` for each story.
- Follow `.claude/rules/tasks-generation.md` when writing tasks.md.
